// error: `*` needs two numbers of one type, not int and Duration
// error: expected long, found Duration
// error: no overload of `/` accepts these arguments; the overloads are `Duration./(n: long)`, `Duration./(other: Duration)`
// error: `+` needs two values of one type, not Duration and int
// error: `*` needs two values of one type, not Instant and int
// A count goes after the duration it scales, never before it; a duration scales by a whole count,
// not another duration or a `real`; a bare number is no duration; and an instant does not scale.
import avin.time.{Instant, seconds}

main()
    println(3 * seconds(1))
    println(seconds(1) * seconds(2))
    println(seconds(1) / 1.5)
    println(seconds(1) + 1)
    println(Instant.Epoch * 2)
